# (the user, 2026-10-28) Sequence 2's octave moves with Motion: Aran (AISLING's; Sequence 2 at -1) at Motion 100 moves
# it an octave at a section change and back at the next; its page's Octave knob shows it (home + the shift), OCT- /
# OCT+ light, the reader says it; the project keeps home. The hand wins: OCT- / OCT+ on its page, or its Octave knob,
# make what the knob shows, a step on, the new home, the shift gone (the times: this run's, deterministic; Aran's
# sections change about every 40 s, the first at ~21 s)
wait 300
turn PRESET 2
wait 500
expect piece 2
spin K3 60
wait 300
expect par15 100
tap SEQ
wait 300
expect view 4
listen
# the first section change (~21 s): up an octave
wait 24000
expect section 1
expect s2shift 1
expect s2knob 0
expect par23 -1
expect litbtn13 1
expect litbtn12 0
said Octave 0
shot shifted.png
# the next (~61 s): home
wait 40000
expect s2shift 0
expect s2knob -1
expect par23 -1
expect litbtn13 0
expect litbtn12 0
# a later one (~101 s): down; OCT+ makes -1 home (a step on from the -2 shown, not from home), the shift gone
wait 40000
expect s2shift -1
expect s2knob -2
expect litbtn12 1
tap OCT+
wait 200
expect s2shift 0
expect par23 -1
expect s2knob -1
said SEQ 2 OCTAVE -1
expect litbtn12 0
expect litbtn13 0
# the next (~141 s): up; the Octave knob turned up makes the 1 it then shows home
wait 40000
expect s2shift 1
expect s2knob 0
expect par23 -1
spin K2 1
wait 200
expect s2shift 0
expect par23 1
expect s2knob 1
expect litbtn12 0
expect litbtn13 1
# (~181 s: from home, so it rolls at once) shifted again; Motion to 0 (HOME's KNOB 3): home at once
wait 40000
expect s2shift !=0
tap HOME
wait 300
spin K3 -100
wait 200
expect par15 0
expect s2shift 0
